@startuml
title Deadlock Playground - Process State Diagram

top to bottom direction

skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam defaultFontSize 13
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam roundcorner 0
skinparam ArrowColor #444444

skinparam state {
  BackgroundColor #FFFFFF
  BorderColor #444444
  FontColor #222222
  StartColor #333333
  EndColor #333333
}

state "RUNNING" as Running
state "WAITING" as Waiting
state "COMPLETED" as Completed
state "TERMINATED" as Terminated

' --------------------------------
' Process initialization
' --------------------------------

[*] --> Running : Scenario configured

' --------------------------------
' Normal execution
' --------------------------------

Running --> Running : Valid request or release\nwith remaining scripted work

Running --> Waiting : Request cannot be granted\nCapacity shortage or unsafe state

Waiting --> Running : Pending request granted\nMore scripted work remains

' --------------------------------
' Process completion
' --------------------------------

Running --> Completed : Final scripted operation succeeds\nRelease remaining holdings

Waiting --> Completed : Final pending scripted request granted\nRelease remaining holdings

' --------------------------------
' Deadlock recovery
' --------------------------------

Waiting --> Running : Preemption recovery\nRollback to script beginning

Running --> Running : Preemption recovery\nReset execution progress

Running --> Terminated : Recovery termination

Waiting --> Terminated : Recovery termination

' --------------------------------
' Scripted prevention violations
' --------------------------------

Running --> Terminated : Invalid scripted operation\nunder prevention rules

Waiting --> Terminated : Script terminated\nfor a prevention violation

' --------------------------------
' Terminal states
' --------------------------------

Completed --> [*]

Terminated --> [*]

' --------------------------------
' Explanatory notes
' --------------------------------

note right of Running
  The process can execute eligible
  manual or scheduled operations.

  A process without a configured
  script remains available for
  manual operations.

  Valid operations do not always
  change the process state.
end note

note right of Waiting
  The process has an outstanding
  resource request.

  Existing holdings are preserved
  unless an enabled prevention
  rule requires their release.

  Deadlocked is a separate flag,
  not an additional process state.
end note

note right of Completed
  All scripted work has finished.

  No pending scripted operations
  or remaining holdings exist.
end note

note right of Terminated
  The process cannot continue.

  Its holdings are released.

  Termination may result from
  recovery or a scripted
  prevention violation.
end note

legend bottom
  PROCESS LIFECYCLE

  RUNNING:
  Process can perform eligible operations.

  WAITING:
  Process has an outstanding request.

  COMPLETED:
  Script finished successfully.

  TERMINATED:
  Process execution stopped.

  Historical navigation restores a
  recorded state rather than executing
  a normal process transition.

  Reset discards the entire scenario.
  It does not transition processes
  individually back to RUNNING.

  Manual prevention rejections do not
  change the existing process state.
endlegend

@enduml
